.TH AUR-REVIEW 1 "2026-10-23" "aur-review" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
aur-review \- triage pending AUR packaging changes with an LLM before building
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aur-review
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.P
.B aur-review
.B \-p
\fIPKG\fR [\fB\-p\fR \fIPKG\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B aur-review
lists the AUR packages with pending upgrades, and for each one diffs the
packaging files at the commit that was last built locally against the current
upstream commit in the paru clone directory.
The diff, the commit log for the range, and a set of automated grep hits are
sent to an OpenAI-compatible chat endpoint (DeepSeek by default) which returns
a verdict of
.BR clean ,
.B review ,
or
.BR danger .
.P
Before the model is consulted, added lines are matched against a fixed list of
known-bad patterns (downloads piped into a shell, base64 payloads, paste and
file-drop hosts, SSH key writes, miners, \fBsudo\fR, world-writable modes,
\fBSKIP\fR checksums, shell rc edits, and so on) and against the
\fI# Maintainer\fR line of the old and new PKGBUILD.
A match in the high-severity group forces a
.B danger
verdict regardless of what the model says.
.P
The script reads only; it never builds, installs, or modifies a package.
It is called by the
.B update
fish function, which aborts the whole upgrade when the exit status is non-zero.
.P
Requirements:
.BR git ,
.BR jq ,
.BR curl ,
and the paru clone cache left by previous builds. Without that cache a package
cannot be diffed and is reported as
.B review
instead.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-p " PKG"
Review only
.IR PKG ,
ignoring
.BR "paru \-Qua" .
May be repeated. Useful for a single package before installing it.
.TP
.BI \-m " MODEL"
Model name sent to the endpoint. Default:
.IR deepseek-flash .
.TP
.B \-n
Dry run. Print the prompt that would be sent, with a byte count, and make no
API call. Requires no key.
.TP
.B \-v
Also print the model's reasons for packages it marked clean.
.TP
.B \-q
Only report problems; suppress the header and the clean lines.
.TP
.B \-h
Show usage and exit.
.SH BEHAVIOUR
.SS What gets diffed
.IP \(bu 2
\fIPKGBUILD\fR, \fI*.install\fR, \fI*.patch\fR, \fI*.diff\fR and \fI*.sh\fR
in \fB~/.cache/paru/clone/\fI<pkg>\fR.
.IP \(bu 2
The range is \fBHEAD\fR (last built) to the tracking branch, after a
\fBgit fetch\fR. If no upstream is configured, \fIorigin/master\fR,
\fIorigin/main\fR, then \fIFETCH_HEAD\fR are tried.
.IP \(bu 2
An empty recipe diff is reported as clean without calling the API.
.IP \(bu 2
Prompts larger than \fBAUR_REVIEW_MAX_DIFF\fR bytes keep the first 60 percent
and the last part of the diff, with the omitted byte count marked inline.
.SS Verdicts
.IP \(bu 2
.B clean
\- nothing security-relevant changed. The upgrade proceeds.
.IP \(bu 2
.B review
\- suspicious or unfamiliar code. The upgrade still proceeds; the reasons
are printed so they can be read, which matters because the
.B update
function runs paru with
.BR \-\-skipreview .
.IP \(bu 2
.B danger
\- malicious or clearly unacceptable. Exit status 1, and
.B update
stops before touching any package.
.SS Requirements
.IP \(bu 2
.BR git ,
.BR jq ,
.BR curl .
.IP \(bu 2
A key in
.I ~/.config/aur-review/key
(mode 0600) or in
.BR AUR_REVIEW_API_KEY .
.IP \(bu 2
.B paru
for the default package list, unless
.B \-p
is given.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B AUR_REVIEW_API_KEY
Key, overriding the key file.
.TP
.B AUR_REVIEW_KEY_FILE
Alternative key file path.
.TP
.B AUR_REVIEW_BASE_URL
API root, default \fIhttps://api.deepseek.com/v1\fR.
.TP
.B AUR_REVIEW_MODEL
Default model name.
.TP
.B AUR_REVIEW_CLONE_DIR
paru clone directory, default \fI~/.cache/paru/clone\fR.
.TP
.B AUR_REVIEW_MAX_DIFF
Prompt size ceiling in bytes, default 40000.
.TP
.B AUR_REVIEW_TIMEOUT
Per-request curl timeout in seconds, default 90.
.SH EXAMPLES
Review everything paru would build:
.IP
.EX
aur-review
.EE
.P
Read the verdicts but keep going with the update anyway:
.IP
.EX
aur-review; paru \-Syu
.EE
.P
Check one package before installing it:
.IP
.EX
aur-review \-p some\-git\-package
.EE
.P
See exactly what would be sent, without spending tokens:
.IP
.EX
aur-review \-n \-p some\-package
.EE
.P
Inspect a flagged diff yourself:
.IP
.EX
git \-C ~/.cache/paru/clone/<pkg> diff HEAD..@{u}
.EE
.P
Upgrade without the review step:
.IP
.EX
update \-\-skip\-ai
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Nothing flagged, or only
.B review
verdicts.
.TP
.B 1
At least one
.B danger
verdict.
.TP
.B 2
Could not scan: missing key, missing dependency, or no pending list.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/aur-review/key
API key, one line, mode 0600.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/paru/clone/
Per-package git checkouts used for the diff.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR paru (8),
.BR pacman (8),
.BR flatpak (1),
.BR git (1)
.SH BUGS
The upstream source tarball is not inspected; only the packaging recipe is.
A clean verdict is not a statement about the code that gets compiled.
The diff is taken against the last commit paru checked out, which can be newer
than the installed version if a build was previously skipped or failed, so a
change may be reviewed twice.
Devel packages (\fI\-git\fR and friends) always show changes and will often be
flagged for reading.
.SH AUTHOR
Written for local use.
